&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;New page&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;__NOTOC__&lt;br /&gt;
'''Release date:''' February 25, 2008&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
* This release is primarily an update that contains the demo shown at GDC.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
* A new enemy character, the spider, has been added to the demo game. Its controller is now the simplest example of a controller for a non-player character.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
* A world can now be paused by setting the &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;kWorldPaused&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; flag with the &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;[http://c4engine.com/docs/WorldMgr/World_SetWorldFlags.html World::SetWorldFlags()]&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; function. (Care should be taken to avoid clearing other flags by calling &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;[http://c4engine.com/docs/WorldMgr/World_GetWorldFlags.html World::GetWorldFlags()]&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; and logically ORing in the &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;kWorldPaused&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; flag.) While this flag is set, controllers and effects are not moved. The demo game now sets this flag when the menu window is displayed in single player mode.&lt;/div&gt;</summary>
